{
  "sstoreReentrancySentryAcrossUpgrades": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "EIP-2200's reentrancy sentry: SSTORE fails outright when 2300 gas or less remains, whatever the write would otherwise cost. This is the reason EIP-2200 exists at all -- EIP-1283 introduced net metering without it and was withdrawn, because a 2300-gas stipend was suddenly enough to write storage and reentrancy guards built on that assumption broke. This chain never ran EIP-1283 and adopted EIP-2200 directly at Phoenix.",
      "eip": "EIP-2200 at Phoenix. The sentry is the ONE part of that rule no gas measurement can reach, because it is a refusal rather than a price.",
      "theProbe": "Two calls to the same helper, doing the same no-op write, differing only in gas: 2300 and 2400. Each call's return status is stored. The PAIR is the assertion -- one must fail and the other must not.",
      "slots": "0x01 status of the 2300-gas call, 0x02 status of the 2400-gas call, 0x1f liveness marker.",
      "whatEachUpgradeSays": "Through Agharta the helper's write is metered legacy-style at 5000 gas, so BOTH calls run out and both statuses are 0. From Phoenix the write is a no-op costing far less than either budget -- so the 2400 call succeeds, and the 2300 call fails ANYWAY. That asymmetry is the sentry and nothing else produces it.",
      "whyAGasReadingCannotSeeThis": "Every other storage fixture here measures what a write COSTS. The sentry sets no price; it refuses. A client that priced every branch of EIP-2200 perfectly and omitted the sentry is indistinguishable from a correct one by any gas figure, which is why this needs a call boundary rather than a GAS bracket.",
      "provenance": "Authored 2026-08-25. Named as open when the SSTORE branch table was audited, then confirmed by wrong build: a client with the sentry condition disabled was passed silently by all 36 state fixtures then in the suite.",
      "oracle": "core-geth's own statetest runner, which is not the implementation under certification.",
      "oracle-version": "core-geth modernized 1.13.0-26975d6a. Production v1.12.21 cannot be used: its t8n fork table has no ETC_DieHard, ETC_Gotham or ETC_DefuseDifficultyBomb.",
      "generated": "2026-08-25",
      "signing": "txbytes carries the signed transaction. Legacy signature through Gas Reprice, replay-protected from Die Hard.",
      "unfilled-no-fork-name": "No expectation for ETC_Thanos: the generator's fork table has no name for it.",
      "unfilled-not-a-state-rule": "No expectation for ETC_DAOFork, ETC_DAOWars, ETC_FrontierThawing, ETC_MESSOff, ETC_MESSOn."
    },
